==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|frm|tendrillon||bud, shoot, cartilage}}, perhaps a diminutive of {{m|frm|tendron||cartilage}}, from {{uder|en|fro|tendre||soft}} (see [[tender]] (adj.)), or else from {{uder|en|la|tendere||to stretch, extend}} (see [[tender]] (v.)).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛn.dɹəl/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tendril.wav|Audio (RP)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} A thin, [[spirally]] [[coiling]] [[stem]] that attaches a [[plant]] to its [[support]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} A [[hair]]-like [[tentacle]].

